LOGBOOK.md:14:- FINDING (missing from the entry below, which stopped at `7a66c73`): the deeper CocoaSkills defect was never Windows-specific. `_validate_namespace_independence` compared every namespace with every other and canonicalised **both** operands per comparison, and the pass re-runs on every journal save — **twice per 32 KiB staging chunk**. One install measured **750,620** canonicalisations, 182 s of its 210 s, *on macOS*. Windows opens a handle per path component for the same question, so only there did quadratic-with-a-cheap-constant become fatal. A POSIX-latent cost defect that a slower syscall promotes to an outage is worth looking for before the next change near a hot revalidation path.
LOGBOOK.md:17:- STATUS: signed `f8b90a5` on `ivanopcode/cocoaskills` only, PR 16 head. **PR 16 run `30641011440` is 14/14 green** — 12 test cells, mypy strict, Build artifacts. Windows cells report **1217 passed / 152 skipped** each (672 / 851 / 493 / 660 s), against 1211 / 152 at `32737a8`. Local: `mypy` strict exit 0 (67 files); focused suites exit 0, 162 passed / 4 skipped; full suite exit 0, **1151 passed / 100 skipped** against a 1145 / 100 baseline — the delta is exactly the six new tests on both. CocoaSkills `LOGBOOK.md` carries the two code reworks; the platform fact above is recorded here rather than there, to avoid churning a green PR head for a documentation line.
LOGBOOK.md:27:- NOTE: independent cross-language corroboration — the CocoaSkills diagnosis (`0x410` directory-junction reparse point; a manager home made by a plain `mkdir` inherits its parent's ACEs and can never satisfy an owner-only de-inherited DACL) matches what `BUG-260731-33v6zz` found in the Go implementation, arrived at separately the same day. Two codebases, two languages, same platform truths.
