LOGBOOK.md:1799:- DECISION: removal is a rename to a private `.sweep-<name>-<random>` sibling inside the same proven root. That rename *is* the atomic removal; the `RemoveAll` behind it is resumable cleanup the next sweep finishes. Both paths are direct children of one validated root, so a deletion cannot escape the cache root even when the entry contains links.
