137706-+paths. Each group includes live, staged, staged-source, backup, rollback, and
137707-+cleanup generations. GC snapshots every candidate before and after reading and
137708-+requires at least one valid marker in every group. A vanished generation group,
137709-+an unreadable journal or marker, or a concurrent generation change makes the
137710-+entire mark phase uncertain and suppresses runtime, snapshot, and build sweeps.
137711-+This prevents a valid marker from one project, global, or hybrid target from
137712-+masking the loss of another in-flight target.
137713-+
137714-+Build retirement is also bound to the object that was classified. The POSIX
137715-+backend compares the inspected directory generation at the held parent
137716-+descriptor, renames through that descriptor, and verifies the quarantined
137717-+inode before deletion. A concurrent entry replacement is restored or retained,
137718-+while a concurrent root replacement leaves the new namespace untouched. The
137719-+Windows backend reopens and records the verified file identity, then uses
137720:+`SetFileInformationByHandle(FileRenameInfo)` with the held quarantine directory
137721-+handle so the rename acts on that exact object without replacing a destination.
137722-+Native backend tests exchange entries and driver roots between classification
137723-+and retirement and assert that young replacements are never deleted.
137724-+
137725-+Runtime orphan cleanup recognizes only the manager-owned legacy and indexed
137726-+temporary/backup names and indexed stale names. PID liveness remains the sweep
137727-+gate; malformed, leading-zero, or unrelated dotfile names are retained.
