243539-+paths. Each group includes live, staged, staged-source, backup, rollback, and
243540-+cleanup generations. GC snapshots every candidate before and after reading and
243541-+requires at least one valid marker in every group. A vanished generation group,
243542-+an unreadable journal or marker, or a concurrent generation change makes the
243543-+entire mark phase uncertain and suppresses runtime, snapshot, and build sweeps.
243544-+This prevents a valid marker from one project, global, or hybrid target from
243545-+masking the loss of another in-flight target.
243546-+
243547-+Build retirement is also bound to the object that was classified. The POSIX
243548-+backend compares the inspected directory generation at the held parent
243549-+descriptor, renames through that descriptor, and verifies the quarantined
243550-+inode before deletion. A concurrent entry replacement is restored or retained,
243551-+while a concurrent root replacement leaves the new namespace untouched. The
243552-+Windows backend reopens and records the verified file identity, then uses
243553:+`SetFileInformationByHandle(FileRenameInfo)` with the held quarantine directory
243554-+handle so the rename acts on that exact object without replacing a destination.
243555-+Native backend tests exchange entries and driver roots between classification
243556-+and retirement and assert that young replacements are never deleted.
243557-+
243558-+Runtime orphan cleanup recognizes only the manager-owned legacy and indexed
