280082-+
280083-+The journal mark boundary is per transaction context target, not a flat set of
280084-+paths. Each group includes live, staged, staged-source, backup, rollback, and
280085-+cleanup generations. GC snapshots every candidate before and after reading and
280086-+requires at least one valid marker in every group. A vanished generation group,
280087-+an unreadable journal or marker, or a concurrent generation change makes the
280088-+entire mark phase uncertain and suppresses runtime, snapshot, and build sweeps.
280089-+This prevents a valid marker from one project, global, or hybrid target from
280090-+masking the loss of another in-flight target.
280091-+
280092-+Build retirement is also bound to the object that was classified. The POSIX
280093-+backend compares the inspected directory generation at the held parent
280094-+descriptor, renames through that descriptor, and verifies the quarantined
280095-+inode before deletion. A concurrent entry replacement is restored or retained,
280096-+while a concurrent root replacement leaves the new namespace untouched. The
280097-+Windows backend reopens and records the verified file identity, then uses
280098:+`SetFileInformationByHandle(FileRenameInfo)` with the held quarantine directory
280099-+handle so the rename acts on that exact object without replacing a destination.
280100-+Native backend tests exchange entries and driver roots between classification
280101-+and retirement and assert that young replacements are never deleted.
