436924-+## Reviewer findings resolved
436925-+
436926-+### In-flight journal generations
436927-+
436928-+Transaction journals now expose marker generations in a separate group for
436929-+each context target. A group covers its live, staged, staged-source, backup,
436930-+rollback, cleanup, and cleanup-tomb paths. GC snapshots those paths before and
436931-+after marker reads, requires at least one valid marker in every group, and
436932-+merges references only from a fully safe group. A missing group, corrupt or
436933-+unreadable marker, path race, journal-root race, or journal filesystem error
--
436938-+vanishing, a generation disappearing during the scan, a forced journal-root
436939-+`OSError`, and one valid project target alongside vanished global and hybrid
436940-+targets so unrelated context state cannot mask uncertainty.
436941-+
436942-+### Exact protected-object retirement
436943-+
436944-+The POSIX collector carries the classified directory state into quarantine,
436945-+selects it through the held driver descriptor, and verifies the quarantined
436946-+inode before deletion. A pathname exchange is restored or retained; a driver
436947-+root exchange can sweep only the entry reached through the previously held
436948-+root descriptor and never the new live root.
436949-+
436950-+The Windows collector reopens and records the verified object identity, opens
436951-+the selected source with `DELETE`, and renames that exact open handle with
436952:+`SetFileInformationByHandle(FileRenameInfo)`. The destination is relative to
436953-+the already-held quarantine directory, and replacement is disabled. Entry and
436954-+root exchange tests plant a valid young replacement between classification and
436955-+retirement and assert that it remains a cache hit.
436956-+
436957-+### Runtime orphan compatibility
436958-+
436959-+Orphan matching is limited to manager-owned legacy and indexed temporary and
436960-+backup names plus indexed stale names. PID and allocation indexes must use the
436961-+canonical numeric shape. Live-PID entries and malformed, leading-zero, or
436962-+unrelated dotfiles are retained; only exact dead-PID names are swept.
436963-+
436964-+### Native Windows coverage
436965-+
436966-+The fake build fixture now derives the native target and artifact suffix on
--
436973-+
436974-+The previously accepted currentness behavior was preserved: marker-v1 schemas
436975-+1–5, raw-snapshot and static-context replanning, complete target/toolchain/
436976-+execution-policy cache identity, protected receipt/artifact and shim checks,
436977-+result-only capability evidence, and normal-install rebuild/repair remain
436978-+unchanged by this rework.
436979-+
