440168-+## Reviewer findings resolved
440169-+
440170-+### In-flight journal generations
440171-+
440172-+Transaction journals now expose marker generations in a separate group for
440173-+each context target. A group covers its live, staged, staged-source, backup,
440174-+rollback, cleanup, and cleanup-tomb paths. GC snapshots those paths before and
440175-+after marker reads, requires at least one valid marker in every group, and
440176-+merges references only from a fully safe group. A missing group, corrupt or
440177-+unreadable marker, path race, journal-root race, or journal filesystem error
--
440182-+vanishing, a generation disappearing during the scan, a forced journal-root
440183-+`OSError`, and one valid project target alongside vanished global and hybrid
440184-+targets so unrelated context state cannot mask uncertainty.
440185-+
440186-+### Exact protected-object retirement
440187-+
440188-+The POSIX collector carries the classified directory state into quarantine,
440189-+selects it through the held driver descriptor, and verifies the quarantined
440190-+inode before deletion. A pathname exchange is restored or retained; a driver
440191-+root exchange can sweep only the entry reached through the previously held
440192-+root descriptor and never the new live root.
440193-+
440194-+The Windows collector reopens and records the verified object identity, opens
440195-+the selected source with `DELETE`, and renames that exact open handle with
440196:+`SetFileInformationByHandle(FileRenameInfo)`. The destination is relative to
440197-+the already-held quarantine directory, and replacement is disabled. Entry and
440198-+root exchange tests plant a valid young replacement between classification and
440199-+retirement and assert that it remains a cache hit.
440200-+
440201-+### Runtime orphan compatibility
440202-+
440203-+Orphan matching is limited to manager-owned legacy and indexed temporary and
440204-+backup names plus indexed stale names. PID and allocation indexes must use the
440205-+canonical numeric shape. Live-PID entries and malformed, leading-zero, or
440206-+unrelated dotfiles are retained; only exact dead-PID names are swept.
440207-+
440208-+### Native Windows coverage
440209-+
440210-+The fake build fixture now derives the native target and artifact suffix on
--
440217-+
440218-+The previously accepted currentness behavior was preserved: marker-v1 schemas
440219-+1–5, raw-snapshot and static-context replanning, complete target/toolchain/
440220-+execution-policy cache identity, protected receipt/artifact and shim checks,
440221-+result-only capability evidence, and normal-install rebuild/repair remain
440222-+unchanged by this rework.
