448277-+## Reviewer findings resolved
448278-+
448279-+### In-flight journal generations
448280-+
448281-+Transaction journals now expose marker generations in a separate group for
448282-+each context target. A group covers its live, staged, staged-source, backup,
448283-+rollback, cleanup, and cleanup-tomb paths. GC snapshots those paths before and
448284-+after marker reads, requires at least one valid marker in every group, and
448285-+merges references only from a fully safe group. A missing group, corrupt or
448286-+unreadable marker, path race, journal-root race, or journal filesystem error
--
448291-+vanishing, a generation disappearing during the scan, a forced journal-root
448292-+`OSError`, and one valid project target alongside vanished global and hybrid
448293-+targets so unrelated context state cannot mask uncertainty.
448294-+
448295-+### Exact protected-object retirement
448296-+
448297-+The POSIX collector carries the classified directory state into quarantine,
448298-+selects it through the held driver descriptor, and verifies the quarantined
448299-+inode before deletion. A pathname exchange is restored or retained; a driver
448300-+root exchange can sweep only the entry reached through the previously held
448301-+root descriptor and never the new live root.
448302-+
448303-+The Windows collector reopens and records the verified object identity, opens
448304-+the selected source with `DELETE`, and renames that exact open handle with
448305:+`SetFileInformationByHandle(FileRenameInfo)`. The destination is relative to
448306-+the already-held quarantine directory, and replacement is disabled. Entry and
448307-+root exchange tests plant a valid young replacement between classification and
448308-+retirement and assert that it remains a cache hit.
448309-+
448310-+### Runtime orphan compatibility
448311-+
448312-+Orphan matching is limited to manager-owned legacy and indexed temporary and
448313-+backup names plus indexed stale names. PID and allocation indexes must use the
448314-+canonical numeric shape. Live-PID entries and malformed, leading-zero, or
448315-+unrelated dotfiles are retained; only exact dead-PID names are swept.
448316-+
448317-+### Native Windows coverage
448318-+
448319-+The fake build fixture now derives the native target and artifact suffix on
