455846-+## Reviewer findings resolved
455847-+
455848-+### In-flight journal generations
455849-+
455850-+Transaction journals now expose marker generations in a separate group for
455851-+each context target. A group covers its live, staged, staged-source, backup,
455852-+rollback, cleanup, and cleanup-tomb paths. GC snapshots those paths before and
455853-+after marker reads, requires at least one valid marker in every group, and
455854-+merges references only from a fully safe group. A missing group, corrupt or
455855-+unreadable marker, path race, journal-root race, or journal filesystem error
--
455860-+vanishing, a generation disappearing during the scan, a forced journal-root
455861-+`OSError`, and one valid project target alongside vanished global and hybrid
455862-+targets so unrelated context state cannot mask uncertainty.
455863-+
455864-+### Exact protected-object retirement
455865-+
455866-+The POSIX collector carries the classified directory state into quarantine,
455867-+selects it through the held driver descriptor, and verifies the quarantined
455868-+inode before deletion. A pathname exchange is restored or retained; a driver
455869-+root exchange can sweep only the entry reached through the previously held
455870-+root descriptor and never the new live root.
455871-+
455872-+The Windows collector reopens and records the verified object identity, opens
455873-+the selected source with `DELETE`, and renames that exact open handle with
455874:+`SetFileInformationByHandle(FileRenameInfo)`. The destination is relative to
455875-+the already-held quarantine directory, and replacement is disabled. Entry and
455876-+root exchange tests plant a valid young replacement between classification and
455877-+retirement and assert that it remains a cache hit.
455878-+
455879-+### Runtime orphan compatibility
455880-+
455881-+Orphan matching is limited to manager-owned legacy and indexed temporary and
455882-+backup names plus indexed stale names. PID and allocation indexes must use the
455883-+canonical numeric shape. Live-PID entries and malformed, leading-zero, or
455884-+unrelated dotfiles are retained; only exact dead-PID names are swept.
455885-+
455886-+### Native Windows coverage
455887-+
455888-+The fake build fixture now derives the native target and artifact suffix on
--
455895-+
455896-+The previously accepted currentness behavior was preserved: marker-v1 schemas
455897-+1–5, raw-snapshot and static-context replanning, complete target/toolchain/
455898-+execution-policy cache identity, protected receipt/artifact and shim checks,
455899-+result-only capability evidence, and normal-install rebuild/repair remain
455900-+unchanged by this rework.
455901-+
455902-+## Fact-checking and sources
455903-+
455904-+- The task behavior remains checked against the Curator manager requirements
455905-+  for [status and locked fail-safe GC](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec/blob/f5d7673039226ab81de2f4f87e2155ae995c4df3/profiles/manager.md#L657-L684),
455906-+  [cache acceptance and rebuild](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec/blob/f5d7673039226ab81de2f4f87e2155ae995c4df3/profiles/manager.md#L329-L340),
455907-+  and [normal-install repair](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec/blob/f5d7673039226ab81de2f4f87e2155ae995c4df3/profiles/manager.md#L444-L463).
455908-+- Microsoft documents that the file handle passed to
455909:+  [`SetFileInformationByHandle`](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/fileapi/nf-fileapi-setfileinformationbyhandle)
455910-+  must carry the access needed for the requested change and that
455911-+  `FileRenameInfo` is the rename information class.
455912-+- Microsoft's
455913-+  [`FILE_RENAME_INFORMATION`](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-hardware/drivers/ddi/ntifs/ns-ntifs-_file_rename_information)
455914-+  contract states that rename acts on the supplied file handle, requires
455915-+  `DELETE` access, can resolve a relative name through a held root-directory
455916-+  handle, and fails on an existing target when replacement is false. It also
455917-+  defines the variable-length buffer sizing used by the implementation.
455918-+
