462326-+## Reviewer findings resolved
462327-+
462328-+### In-flight journal generations
462329-+
462330-+Transaction journals now expose marker generations in a separate group for
462331-+each context target. A group covers its live, staged, staged-source, backup,
462332-+rollback, cleanup, and cleanup-tomb paths. GC snapshots those paths before and
462333-+after marker reads, requires at least one valid marker in every group, and
462334-+merges references only from a fully safe group. A missing group, corrupt or
462335-+unreadable marker, path race, journal-root race, or journal filesystem error
--
462340-+vanishing, a generation disappearing during the scan, a forced journal-root
462341-+`OSError`, and one valid project target alongside vanished global and hybrid
462342-+targets so unrelated context state cannot mask uncertainty.
462343-+
462344-+### Exact protected-object retirement
462345-+
462346-+The POSIX collector carries the classified directory state into quarantine,
462347-+selects it through the held driver descriptor, and verifies the quarantined
462348-+inode before deletion. A pathname exchange is restored or retained; a driver
462349-+root exchange can sweep only the entry reached through the previously held
462350-+root descriptor and never the new live root.
462351-+
462352-+The Windows collector reopens and records the verified object identity, opens
462353-+the selected source with `DELETE`, and renames that exact open handle with
462354:+`SetFileInformationByHandle(FileRenameInfo)`. The destination is relative to
462355-+the already-held quarantine directory, and replacement is disabled. Entry and
462356-+root exchange tests plant a valid young replacement between classification and
462357-+retirement and assert that it remains a cache hit.
462358-+
462359-+### Runtime orphan compatibility
462360-+
462361-+Orphan matching is limited to manager-owned legacy and indexed temporary and
462362-+backup names plus indexed stale names. PID and allocation indexes must use the
462363-+canonical numeric shape. Live-PID entries and malformed, leading-zero, or
462364-+unrelated dotfiles are retained; only exact dead-PID names are swept.
462365-+
462366-+### Native Windows coverage
462367-+
462368-+The fake build fixture now derives the native target and artifact suffix on
--
