465566-+## Reviewer findings resolved
465567-+
465568-+### In-flight journal generations
465569-+
465570-+Transaction journals now expose marker generations in a separate group for
465571-+each context target. A group covers its live, staged, staged-source, backup,
465572-+rollback, cleanup, and cleanup-tomb paths. GC snapshots those paths before and
465573-+after marker reads, requires at least one valid marker in every group, and
465574-+merges references only from a fully safe group. A missing group, corrupt or
465575-+unreadable marker, path race, journal-root race, or journal filesystem error
--
465580-+vanishing, a generation disappearing during the scan, a forced journal-root
465581-+`OSError`, and one valid project target alongside vanished global and hybrid
465582-+targets so unrelated context state cannot mask uncertainty.
465583-+
465584-+### Exact protected-object retirement
465585-+
465586-+The POSIX collector carries the classified directory state into quarantine,
465587-+selects it through the held driver descriptor, and verifies the quarantined
465588-+inode before deletion. A pathname exchange is restored or retained; a driver
465589-+root exchange can sweep only the entry reached through the previously held
465590-+root descriptor and never the new live root.
465591-+
465592-+The Windows collector reopens and records the verified object identity, opens
465593-+the selected source with `DELETE`, and renames that exact open handle with
465594:+`SetFileInformationByHandle(FileRenameInfo)`. The destination is relative to
465595-+the already-held quarantine directory, and replacement is disabled. Entry and
465596-+root exchange tests plant a valid young replacement between classification and
465597-+retirement and assert that it remains a cache hit.
465598-+
465599-+### Runtime orphan compatibility
465600-+
465601-+Orphan matching is limited to manager-owned legacy and indexed temporary and
465602-+backup names plus indexed stale names. PID and allocation indexes must use the
465603-+canonical numeric shape. Live-PID entries and malformed, leading-zero, or
465604-+unrelated dotfiles are retained; only exact dead-PID names are swept.
465605-+
465606-+### Native Windows coverage
465607-+
465608-+The fake build fixture now derives the native target and artifact suffix on
--
465615-+
465616-+The previously accepted currentness behavior was preserved: marker-v1 schemas
465617-+1–5, raw-snapshot and static-context replanning, complete target/toolchain/
465618-+execution-policy cache identity, protected receipt/artifact and shim checks,
465619-+result-only capability evidence, and normal-install rebuild/repair remain
465620-+unchanged by this rework.
465621-+
465622-+## Fact-checking and sources
465623-+
465624-+- The task behavior remains checked against the Curator manager requirements
465625-+  for [status and locked fail-safe GC](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec/blob/f5d7673039226ab81de2f4f87e2155ae995c4df3/profiles/manager.md#L657-L684),
465626-+  [cache acceptance and rebuild](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec/blob/f5d7673039226ab81de2f4f87e2155ae995c4df3/profiles/manager.md#L329-L340),
465627-+  and [normal-install repair](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec/blob/f5d7673039226ab81de2f4f87e2155ae995c4df3/profiles/manager.md#L444-L463).
465628-+- Microsoft documents that the file handle passed to
465629:+  [`SetFileInformationByHandle`](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/fileapi/nf-fileapi-setfileinformationbyhandle)
465630-+  must carry the access needed for the requested change and that
465631-+  `FileRenameInfo` is the rename information class.
465632-+- Microsoft's
465633-+  [`FILE_RENAME_INFORMATION`](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-hardware/drivers/ddi/ntifs/ns-ntifs-_file_rename_information)
465634-+  contract states that rename acts on the supplied file handle, requires
465635-+  `DELETE` access, can resolve a relative name through a held root-directory
465636-+  handle, and fails on an existing target when replacement is false. It also
465637-+  defines the variable-length buffer sizing used by the implementation.
465638-+
