467224-+# TASK-260720-th0jdi — Review rework evidence (RUN-260801-a7ef1b)
467225-+
467226-+## Provenance
467227-+
467228-+- Task: `TASK-260720-th0jdi` — Implement build currentness, repair, and GC.
467229-+- Recorded clean base and merge base: `07655553cebcf867bbe58629de98e77644606c85`.
467230-+- Previously reviewed head: `f3c1254e4fe7958c720cbef096a4ef00103d43a2`.
467231:+- Rework head: `0314ab5939b51cf33f0fdbb68c9df90631e84f5a`.
467232-+- `git verify-commit HEAD` exited `0` with a good ECDSA signature for `oparin@me.com`.
467233-+- Existing pull request: [ivanopcode/cocoaskills#18](https://github.com/ivanopcode/cocoaskills/pull/18).
467234-+- Exact-head GitHub Actions run: [30679822247](https://github.com/ivanopcode/cocoaskills/actions/runs/30679822247) — **pending at artifact draft time**.
467235-+
467236-+## Reviewer findings resolved
467237-+
467238-+### In-flight journal generations
467239-+
467240-+Transaction journals now expose marker generations in a separate group for
467241-+each context target. A group covers its live, staged, staged-source, backup,
467242-+rollback, cleanup, and cleanup-tomb paths. GC snapshots those paths before and
467243-+after marker reads, requires at least one valid marker in every group, and
467244-+merges references only from a fully safe group. A missing group, corrupt or
467245-+unreadable marker, path race, journal-root race, or journal filesystem error
--
467250-+vanishing, a generation disappearing during the scan, a forced journal-root
467251-+`OSError`, and one valid project target alongside vanished global and hybrid
467252-+targets so unrelated context state cannot mask uncertainty.
467253-+
467254-+### Exact protected-object retirement
467255-+
467256-+The POSIX collector carries the classified directory state into quarantine,
467257-+selects it through the held driver descriptor, and verifies the quarantined
467258-+inode before deletion. A pathname exchange is restored or retained; a driver
467259-+root exchange can sweep only the entry reached through the previously held
467260-+root descriptor and never the new live root.
467261-+
467262-+The Windows collector reopens and records the verified object identity, opens
467263-+the selected source with `DELETE`, and renames that exact open handle with
467264:+`SetFileInformationByHandle(FileRenameInfo)`. The destination is relative to
467265-+the already-held quarantine directory, and replacement is disabled. Entry and
467266-+root exchange tests plant a valid young replacement between classification and
467267-+retirement and assert that it remains a cache hit.
467268-+
467269-+### Runtime orphan compatibility
467270-+
467271-+Orphan matching is limited to manager-owned legacy and indexed temporary and
467272-+backup names plus indexed stale names. PID and allocation indexes must use the
467273-+canonical numeric shape. Live-PID entries and malformed, leading-zero, or
467274-+unrelated dotfiles are retained; only exact dead-PID names are swept.
467275-+
467276-+### Native Windows coverage
467277-+
467278-+The fake build fixture now derives the native target and artifact suffix on
--
467285-+
467286-+The previously accepted currentness behavior was preserved: marker-v1 schemas
467287-+1–5, raw-snapshot and static-context replanning, complete target/toolchain/
467288-+execution-policy cache identity, protected receipt/artifact and shim checks,
467289-+result-only capability evidence, and normal-install rebuild/repair remain
467290-+unchanged by this rework.
467291-+
467292-+## Fact-checking and sources
467293-+
467294-+- The task behavior remains checked against the Curator manager requirements
467295-+  for [status and locked fail-safe GC](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec/blob/f5d7673039226ab81de2f4f87e2155ae995c4df3/profiles/manager.md#L657-L684),
467296-+  [cache acceptance and rebuild](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec/blob/f5d7673039226ab81de2f4f87e2155ae995c4df3/profiles/manager.md#L329-L340),
467297-+  and [normal-install repair](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec/blob/f5d7673039226ab81de2f4f87e2155ae995c4df3/profiles/manager.md#L444-L463).
467298-+- Microsoft documents that the file handle passed to
467299:+  [`SetFileInformationByHandle`](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/fileapi/nf-fileapi-setfileinformationbyhandle)
467300-+  must carry the access needed for the requested change and that
467301-+  `FileRenameInfo` is the rename information class.
467302-+- Microsoft's
467303-+  [`FILE_RENAME_INFORMATION`](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-hardware/drivers/ddi/ntifs/ns-ntifs-_file_rename_information)
467304-+  contract states that rename acts on the supplied file handle, requires
467305-+  `DELETE` access, can resolve a relative name through a held root-directory
467306-+  handle, and fails on an existing target when replacement is false. It also
467307-+  defines the variable-length buffer sizing used by the implementation.
467308-+
