478451-+# TASK-260720-th0jdi — Review rework evidence (RUN-260801-a7ef1b)
478452-+
478453-+## Provenance
478454-+
478455-+- Task: `TASK-260720-th0jdi` — Implement build currentness, repair, and GC.
478456-+- Recorded clean base and merge base: `07655553cebcf867bbe58629de98e77644606c85`.
478457-+- Previously reviewed head: `f3c1254e4fe7958c720cbef096a4ef00103d43a2`.
478458:+- Rework head: `0314ab5939b51cf33f0fdbb68c9df90631e84f5a`.
478459-+- `git verify-commit HEAD` exited `0` with a good ECDSA signature for `oparin@me.com`.
478460-+- Existing pull request: [ivanopcode/cocoaskills#18](https://github.com/ivanopcode/cocoaskills/pull/18).
478461-+- Exact-head GitHub Actions run: [30679822247](https://github.com/ivanopcode/cocoaskills/actions/runs/30679822247) — **pending at artifact draft time**.
478462-+
478463-+## Reviewer findings resolved
478464-+
478465-+### In-flight journal generations
478466-+
478467-+Transaction journals now expose marker generations in a separate group for
478468-+each context target. A group covers its live, staged, staged-source, backup,
478469-+rollback, cleanup, and cleanup-tomb paths. GC snapshots those paths before and
478470-+after marker reads, requires at least one valid marker in every group, and
478471-+merges references only from a fully safe group. A missing group, corrupt or
478472-+unreadable marker, path race, journal-root race, or journal filesystem error
--
478477-+vanishing, a generation disappearing during the scan, a forced journal-root
478478-+`OSError`, and one valid project target alongside vanished global and hybrid
478479-+targets so unrelated context state cannot mask uncertainty.
478480-+
478481-+### Exact protected-object retirement
478482-+
478483-+The POSIX collector carries the classified directory state into quarantine,
478484-+selects it through the held driver descriptor, and verifies the quarantined
478485-+inode before deletion. A pathname exchange is restored or retained; a driver
478486-+root exchange can sweep only the entry reached through the previously held
478487-+root descriptor and never the new live root.
478488-+
478489-+The Windows collector reopens and records the verified object identity, opens
478490-+the selected source with `DELETE`, and renames that exact open handle with
478491:+`SetFileInformationByHandle(FileRenameInfo)`. The destination is relative to
478492-+the already-held quarantine directory, and replacement is disabled. Entry and
478493-+root exchange tests plant a valid young replacement between classification and
478494-+retirement and assert that it remains a cache hit.
478495-+
478496-+### Runtime orphan compatibility
478497-+
478498-+Orphan matching is limited to manager-owned legacy and indexed temporary and
478499-+backup names plus indexed stale names. PID and allocation indexes must use the
478500-+canonical numeric shape. Live-PID entries and malformed, leading-zero, or
478501-+unrelated dotfiles are retained; only exact dead-PID names are swept.
478502-+
478503-+### Native Windows coverage
478504-+
478505-+The fake build fixture now derives the native target and artifact suffix on
--
478512-+
478513-+The previously accepted currentness behavior was preserved: marker-v1 schemas
478514-+1–5, raw-snapshot and static-context replanning, complete target/toolchain/
478515-+execution-policy cache identity, protected receipt/artifact and shim checks,
478516-+result-only capability evidence, and normal-install rebuild/repair remain
478517-+unchanged by this rework.
478518-+
478519-+## Fact-checking and sources
478520-+
478521-+- The task behavior remains checked against the Curator manager requirements
478522-+  for [status and locked fail-safe GC](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec/blob/f5d7673039226ab81de2f4f87e2155ae995c4df3/profiles/manager.md#L657-L684),
478523-+  [cache acceptance and rebuild](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec/blob/f5d7673039226ab81de2f4f87e2155ae995c4df3/profiles/manager.md#L329-L340),
478524-+  and [normal-install repair](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec/blob/f5d7673039226ab81de2f4f87e2155ae995c4df3/profiles/manager.md#L444-L463).
478525-+- Microsoft documents that the file handle passed to
478526:+  [`SetFileInformationByHandle`](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/fileapi/nf-fileapi-setfileinformationbyhandle)
478527-+  must carry the access needed for the requested change and that
478528-+  `FileRenameInfo` is the rename information class.
478529-+- Microsoft's
478530-+  [`FILE_RENAME_INFORMATION`](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-hardware/drivers/ddi/ntifs/ns-ntifs-_file_rename_information)
478531-+  contract states that rename acts on the supplied file handle, requires
478532-+  `DELETE` access, can resolve a relative name through a held root-directory
478533-+  handle, and fails on an existing target when replacement is false. It also
478534-+  defines the variable-length buffer sizing used by the implementation.
478535-+
478536-+## Validation evidence
478537-+
478538-+Every gate below was launched as a standalone process without `tee` or an
478539-+exit-status-obscuring pipe.
478540-+
