480343-+## Reviewer findings resolved
480344-+
480345-+### In-flight journal generations
480346-+
480347-+Transaction journals now expose marker generations in a separate group for
480348-+each context target. A group covers its live, staged, staged-source, backup,
480349-+rollback, cleanup, and cleanup-tomb paths. GC snapshots those paths before and
480350-+after marker reads, requires at least one valid marker in every group, and
480351-+merges references only from a fully safe group. A missing group, corrupt or
480352-+unreadable marker, path race, journal-root race, or journal filesystem error
--
480357-+vanishing, a generation disappearing during the scan, a forced journal-root
480358-+`OSError`, and one valid project target alongside vanished global and hybrid
480359-+targets so unrelated context state cannot mask uncertainty.
480360-+
480361-+### Exact protected-object retirement
480362-+
480363-+The POSIX collector carries the classified directory state into quarantine,
480364-+selects it through the held driver descriptor, and verifies the quarantined
480365-+inode before deletion. A pathname exchange is restored or retained; a driver
480366-+root exchange can sweep only the entry reached through the previously held
480367-+root descriptor and never the new live root.
480368-+
480369-+The Windows collector reopens and records the verified object identity, opens
480370-+the selected source with `DELETE`, and renames that exact open handle with
480371:+`SetFileInformationByHandle(FileRenameInfo)`. The destination is relative to
480372-+the already-held quarantine directory, and replacement is disabled. Entry and
480373-+root exchange tests plant a valid young replacement between classification and
480374-+retirement and assert that it remains a cache hit.
480375-+
480376-+### Runtime orphan compatibility
480377-+
480378-+Orphan matching is limited to manager-owned legacy and indexed temporary and
480379-+backup names plus indexed stale names. PID and allocation indexes must use the
480380-+canonical numeric shape. Live-PID entries and malformed, leading-zero, or
480381-+unrelated dotfiles are retained; only exact dead-PID names are swept.
480382-+
480383-+### Native Windows coverage
480384-+
480385-+The fake build fixture now derives the native target and artifact suffix on
--
480392-+
480393-+The previously accepted currentness behavior was preserved: marker-v1 schemas
480394-+1–5, raw-snapshot and static-context replanning, complete target/toolchain/
480395-+execution-policy cache identity, protected receipt/artifact and shim checks,
480396-+result-only capability evidence, and normal-install rebuild/repair remain
480397-+unchanged by this rework.
