480399-+## Fact-checking and sources
480400-+
480401-+- The task behavior remains checked against the Curator manager requirements
480402-+  for [status and locked fail-safe GC](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec/blob/f5d7673039226ab81de2f4f87e2155ae995c4df3/profiles/manager.md#L657-L684),
480403-+  [cache acceptance and rebuild](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec/blob/f5d7673039226ab81de2f4f87e2155ae995c4df3/profiles/manager.md#L329-L340),
480404-+  and [normal-install repair](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec/blob/f5d7673039226ab81de2f4f87e2155ae995c4df3/profiles/manager.md#L444-L463).
480405-+- Microsoft documents that the file handle passed to
480406:+  [`SetFileInformationByHandle`](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/fileapi/nf-fileapi-setfileinformationbyhandle)
480407-+  must carry the access needed for the requested change and that
480408-+  `FileRenameInfo` is the rename information class.
480409-+- Microsoft's
480410-+  [`FILE_RENAME_INFORMATION`](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-hardware/drivers/ddi/ntifs/ns-ntifs-_file_rename_information)
480411-+  contract states that rename acts on the supplied file handle, requires
480412-+  `DELETE` access, can resolve a relative name through a held root-directory
480413-+  handle, and fails on an existing target when replacement is false. It also
480414-+  defines the variable-length buffer sizing used by the implementation.
