485566-+## Reviewer findings resolved
485567-+
485568-+### In-flight journal generations
485569-+
485570-+Transaction journals now expose marker generations in a separate group for
485571-+each context target. A group covers its live, staged, staged-source, backup,
485572-+rollback, cleanup, and cleanup-tomb paths. GC snapshots those paths before and
485573-+after marker reads, requires at least one valid marker in every group, and
485574-+merges references only from a fully safe group. A missing group, corrupt or
485575-+unreadable marker, path race, journal-root race, or journal filesystem error
--
485580-+vanishing, a generation disappearing during the scan, a forced journal-root
485581-+`OSError`, and one valid project target alongside vanished global and hybrid
485582-+targets so unrelated context state cannot mask uncertainty.
485583-+
485584-+### Exact protected-object retirement
485585-+
485586-+The POSIX collector carries the classified directory state into quarantine,
485587-+selects it through the held driver descriptor, and verifies the quarantined
485588-+inode before deletion. A pathname exchange is restored or retained; a driver
485589-+root exchange can sweep only the entry reached through the previously held
485590-+root descriptor and never the new live root.
485591-+
485592-+The Windows collector reopens and records the verified object identity, opens
485593-+the selected source with `DELETE`, and renames that exact open handle with
485594:+`SetFileInformationByHandle(FileRenameInfo)`. The destination is relative to
485595-+the already-held quarantine directory, and replacement is disabled. Entry and
485596-+root exchange tests plant a valid young replacement between classification and
485597-+retirement and assert that it remains a cache hit.
485598-+
485599-+### Runtime orphan compatibility
485600-+
485601-+Orphan matching is limited to manager-owned legacy and indexed temporary and
485602-+backup names plus indexed stale names. PID and allocation indexes must use the
485603-+canonical numeric shape. Live-PID entries and malformed, leading-zero, or
485604-+unrelated dotfiles are retained; only exact dead-PID names are swept.
485605-+
485606-+### Native Windows coverage
485607-+
485608-+The fake build fixture now derives the native target and artifact suffix on
