490581-+## Reviewer findings resolved
490582-+
490583-+### In-flight journal generations
490584-+
490585-+Transaction journals now expose marker generations in a separate group for
490586-+each context target. A group covers its live, staged, staged-source, backup,
490587-+rollback, cleanup, and cleanup-tomb paths. GC snapshots those paths before and
490588-+after marker reads, requires at least one valid marker in every group, and
490589-+merges references only from a fully safe group. A missing group, corrupt or
490590-+unreadable marker, path race, journal-root race, or journal filesystem error
--
490595-+vanishing, a generation disappearing during the scan, a forced journal-root
490596-+`OSError`, and one valid project target alongside vanished global and hybrid
490597-+targets so unrelated context state cannot mask uncertainty.
490598-+
490599-+### Exact protected-object retirement
490600-+
490601-+The POSIX collector carries the classified directory state into quarantine,
490602-+selects it through the held driver descriptor, and verifies the quarantined
490603-+inode before deletion. A pathname exchange is restored or retained; a driver
490604-+root exchange can sweep only the entry reached through the previously held
490605-+root descriptor and never the new live root.
490606-+
490607-+The Windows collector reopens and records the verified object identity, opens
490608-+the selected source with `DELETE`, and renames that exact open handle with
490609:+`SetFileInformationByHandle(FileRenameInfo)`. The destination is relative to
490610-+the already-held quarantine directory, and replacement is disabled. Entry and
490611-+root exchange tests plant a valid young replacement between classification and
490612-+retirement and assert that it remains a cache hit.
490613-+
490614-+### Runtime orphan compatibility
490615-+
490616-+Orphan matching is limited to manager-owned legacy and indexed temporary and
490617-+backup names plus indexed stale names. PID and allocation indexes must use the
490618-+canonical numeric shape. Live-PID entries and malformed, leading-zero, or
490619-+unrelated dotfiles are retained; only exact dead-PID names are swept.
490620-+
490621-+### Native Windows coverage
490622-+
490623-+The fake build fixture now derives the native target and artifact suffix on
--
490630-+
490631-+The previously accepted currentness behavior was preserved: marker-v1 schemas
490632-+1–5, raw-snapshot and static-context replanning, complete target/toolchain/
490633-+execution-policy cache identity, protected receipt/artifact and shim checks,
490634-+result-only capability evidence, and normal-install rebuild/repair remain
490635-+unchanged by this rework.
