498676-+## Reviewer findings resolved
498677-+
498678-+### In-flight journal generations
498679-+
498680-+Transaction journals now expose marker generations in a separate group for
498681-+each context target. A group covers its live, staged, staged-source, backup,
498682-+rollback, cleanup, and cleanup-tomb paths. GC snapshots those paths before and
498683-+after marker reads, requires at least one valid marker in every group, and
498684-+merges references only from a fully safe group. A missing group, corrupt or
498685-+unreadable marker, path race, journal-root race, or journal filesystem error
--
498690-+vanishing, a generation disappearing during the scan, a forced journal-root
498691-+`OSError`, and one valid project target alongside vanished global and hybrid
498692-+targets so unrelated context state cannot mask uncertainty.
498693-+
498694-+### Exact protected-object retirement
498695-+
498696-+The POSIX collector carries the classified directory state into quarantine,
498697-+selects it through the held driver descriptor, and verifies the quarantined
498698-+inode before deletion. A pathname exchange is restored or retained; a driver
498699-+root exchange can sweep only the entry reached through the previously held
498700-+root descriptor and never the new live root.
498701-+
498702-+The Windows collector reopens and records the verified object identity, opens
498703-+the selected source with `DELETE`, and renames that exact open handle with
498704:+`SetFileInformationByHandle(FileRenameInfo)`. The destination is relative to
498705-+the already-held quarantine directory, and replacement is disabled. Entry and
498706-+root exchange tests plant a valid young replacement between classification and
498707-+retirement and assert that it remains a cache hit.
498708-+
498709-+### Runtime orphan compatibility
498710-+
498711-+Orphan matching is limited to manager-owned legacy and indexed temporary and
498712-+backup names plus indexed stale names. PID and allocation indexes must use the
498713-+canonical numeric shape. Live-PID entries and malformed, leading-zero, or
498714-+unrelated dotfiles are retained; only exact dead-PID names are swept.
498715-+
498716-+### Native Windows coverage
498717-+
498718-+The fake build fixture now derives the native target and artifact suffix on
