501872-+## Reviewer findings resolved
501873-+
501874-+### In-flight journal generations
501875-+
501876-+Transaction journals now expose marker generations in a separate group for
501877-+each context target. A group covers its live, staged, staged-source, backup,
501878-+rollback, cleanup, and cleanup-tomb paths. GC snapshots those paths before and
501879-+after marker reads, requires at least one valid marker in every group, and
501880-+merges references only from a fully safe group. A missing group, corrupt or
501881-+unreadable marker, path race, journal-root race, or journal filesystem error
--
501886-+vanishing, a generation disappearing during the scan, a forced journal-root
501887-+`OSError`, and one valid project target alongside vanished global and hybrid
501888-+targets so unrelated context state cannot mask uncertainty.
501889-+
501890-+### Exact protected-object retirement
501891-+
501892-+The POSIX collector carries the classified directory state into quarantine,
501893-+selects it through the held driver descriptor, and verifies the quarantined
501894-+inode before deletion. A pathname exchange is restored or retained; a driver
501895-+root exchange can sweep only the entry reached through the previously held
501896-+root descriptor and never the new live root.
501897-+
501898-+The Windows collector reopens and records the verified object identity, opens
501899-+the selected source with `DELETE`, and renames that exact open handle with
501900:+`SetFileInformationByHandle(FileRenameInfo)`. The destination is relative to
501901-+the already-held quarantine directory, and replacement is disabled. Entry and
501902-+root exchange tests plant a valid young replacement between classification and
501903-+retirement and assert that it remains a cache hit.
501904-+
501905-+### Runtime orphan compatibility
501906-+
501907-+Orphan matching is limited to manager-owned legacy and indexed temporary and
501908-+backup names plus indexed stale names. PID and allocation indexes must use the
501909-+canonical numeric shape. Live-PID entries and malformed, leading-zero, or
501910-+unrelated dotfiles are retained; only exact dead-PID names are swept.
501911-+
501912-+### Native Windows coverage
501913-+
501914-+The fake build fixture now derives the native target and artifact suffix on
