506663-+# TASK-260720-th0jdi — Review rework evidence (RUN-260801-a7ef1b)
506664-+
506665-+## Provenance
506666-+
506667-+- Task: `TASK-260720-th0jdi` — Implement build currentness, repair, and GC.
506668-+- Recorded clean base and merge base: `07655553cebcf867bbe58629de98e77644606c85`.
506669-+- Previously reviewed head: `f3c1254e4fe7958c720cbef096a4ef00103d43a2`.
506670:+- Rework head: `0314ab5939b51cf33f0fdbb68c9df90631e84f5a`.
506671-+- `git verify-commit HEAD` exited `0` with a good ECDSA signature for `oparin@me.com`.
506672-+- Existing pull request: [ivanopcode/cocoaskills#18](https://github.com/ivanopcode/cocoaskills/pull/18).
506673-+- Exact-head GitHub Actions run: [30679822247](https://github.com/ivanopcode/cocoaskills/actions/runs/30679822247) — **pending at artifact draft time**.
506674-+
506675-+## Reviewer findings resolved
506676-+
506677-+### In-flight journal generations
506678-+
506679-+Transaction journals now expose marker generations in a separate group for
506680-+each context target. A group covers its live, staged, staged-source, backup,
506681-+rollback, cleanup, and cleanup-tomb paths. GC snapshots those paths before and
506682-+after marker reads, requires at least one valid marker in every group, and
506683-+merges references only from a fully safe group. A missing group, corrupt or
506684-+unreadable marker, path race, journal-root race, or journal filesystem error
--
506689-+vanishing, a generation disappearing during the scan, a forced journal-root
506690-+`OSError`, and one valid project target alongside vanished global and hybrid
506691-+targets so unrelated context state cannot mask uncertainty.
506692-+
506693-+### Exact protected-object retirement
506694-+
506695-+The POSIX collector carries the classified directory state into quarantine,
506696-+selects it through the held driver descriptor, and verifies the quarantined
506697-+inode before deletion. A pathname exchange is restored or retained; a driver
506698-+root exchange can sweep only the entry reached through the previously held
506699-+root descriptor and never the new live root.
506700-+
506701-+The Windows collector reopens and records the verified object identity, opens
506702-+the selected source with `DELETE`, and renames that exact open handle with
506703:+`SetFileInformationByHandle(FileRenameInfo)`. The destination is relative to
506704-+the already-held quarantine directory, and replacement is disabled. Entry and
506705-+root exchange tests plant a valid young replacement between classification and
506706-+retirement and assert that it remains a cache hit.
506707-+
506708-+### Runtime orphan compatibility
506709-+
506710-+Orphan matching is limited to manager-owned legacy and indexed temporary and
506711-+backup names plus indexed stale names. PID and allocation indexes must use the
506712-+canonical numeric shape. Live-PID entries and malformed, leading-zero, or
506713-+unrelated dotfiles are retained; only exact dead-PID names are swept.
506714-+
506715-+### Native Windows coverage
506716-+
506717-+The fake build fixture now derives the native target and artifact suffix on
--
506724-+
506725-+The previously accepted currentness behavior was preserved: marker-v1 schemas
506726-+1–5, raw-snapshot and static-context replanning, complete target/toolchain/
506727-+execution-policy cache identity, protected receipt/artifact and shim checks,
506728-+result-only capability evidence, and normal-install rebuild/repair remain
506729-+unchanged by this rework.
506730-+
506731-+## Fact-checking and sources
506732-+
506733-+- The task behavior remains checked against the Curator manager requirements
506734-+  for [status and locked fail-safe GC](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec/blob/f5d7673039226ab81de2f4f87e2155ae995c4df3/profiles/manager.md#L657-L684),
506735-+  [cache acceptance and rebuild](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec/blob/f5d7673039226ab81de2f4f87e2155ae995c4df3/profiles/manager.md#L329-L340),
506736-+  and [normal-install repair](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec/blob/f5d7673039226ab81de2f4f87e2155ae995c4df3/profiles/manager.md#L444-L463).
506737-+- Microsoft documents that the file handle passed to
506738:+  [`SetFileInformationByHandle`](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/fileapi/nf-fileapi-setfileinformationbyhandle)
506739-+  must carry the access needed for the requested change and that
506740-+  `FileRenameInfo` is the rename information class.
506741-+- Microsoft's
506742-+  [`FILE_RENAME_INFORMATION`](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-hardware/drivers/ddi/ntifs/ns-ntifs-_file_rename_information)
506743-+  contract states that rename acts on the supplied file handle, requires
506744-+  `DELETE` access, can resolve a relative name through a held root-directory
506745-+  handle, and fails on an existing target when replacement is false. It also
506746-+  defines the variable-length buffer sizing used by the implementation.
