511471-+## Reviewer findings resolved
511472-+
511473-+### In-flight journal generations
511474-+
511475-+Transaction journals now expose marker generations in a separate group for
511476-+each context target. A group covers its live, staged, staged-source, backup,
511477-+rollback, cleanup, and cleanup-tomb paths. GC snapshots those paths before and
511478-+after marker reads, requires at least one valid marker in every group, and
511479-+merges references only from a fully safe group. A missing group, corrupt or
511480-+unreadable marker, path race, journal-root race, or journal filesystem error
--
511485-+vanishing, a generation disappearing during the scan, a forced journal-root
511486-+`OSError`, and one valid project target alongside vanished global and hybrid
511487-+targets so unrelated context state cannot mask uncertainty.
511488-+
511489-+### Exact protected-object retirement
511490-+
511491-+The POSIX collector carries the classified directory state into quarantine,
511492-+selects it through the held driver descriptor, and verifies the quarantined
511493-+inode before deletion. A pathname exchange is restored or retained; a driver
511494-+root exchange can sweep only the entry reached through the previously held
511495-+root descriptor and never the new live root.
511496-+
511497-+The Windows collector reopens and records the verified object identity, opens
511498-+the selected source with `DELETE`, and renames that exact open handle with
511499:+`SetFileInformationByHandle(FileRenameInfo)`. The destination is relative to
511500-+the already-held quarantine directory, and replacement is disabled. Entry and
511501-+root exchange tests plant a valid young replacement between classification and
511502-+retirement and assert that it remains a cache hit.
511503-+
511504-+### Runtime orphan compatibility
511505-+
511506-+Orphan matching is limited to manager-owned legacy and indexed temporary and
511507-+backup names plus indexed stale names. PID and allocation indexes must use the
511508-+canonical numeric shape. Live-PID entries and malformed, leading-zero, or
511509-+unrelated dotfiles are retained; only exact dead-PID names are swept.
511510-+
511511-+### Native Windows coverage
511512-+
511513-+The fake build fixture now derives the native target and artifact suffix on
