514667-+## Reviewer findings resolved
514668-+
514669-+### In-flight journal generations
514670-+
514671-+Transaction journals now expose marker generations in a separate group for
514672-+each context target. A group covers its live, staged, staged-source, backup,
514673-+rollback, cleanup, and cleanup-tomb paths. GC snapshots those paths before and
514674-+after marker reads, requires at least one valid marker in every group, and
514675-+merges references only from a fully safe group. A missing group, corrupt or
514676-+unreadable marker, path race, journal-root race, or journal filesystem error
--
514681-+vanishing, a generation disappearing during the scan, a forced journal-root
514682-+`OSError`, and one valid project target alongside vanished global and hybrid
514683-+targets so unrelated context state cannot mask uncertainty.
514684-+
514685-+### Exact protected-object retirement
514686-+
514687-+The POSIX collector carries the classified directory state into quarantine,
514688-+selects it through the held driver descriptor, and verifies the quarantined
514689-+inode before deletion. A pathname exchange is restored or retained; a driver
514690-+root exchange can sweep only the entry reached through the previously held
514691-+root descriptor and never the new live root.
514692-+
514693-+The Windows collector reopens and records the verified object identity, opens
514694-+the selected source with `DELETE`, and renames that exact open handle with
514695:+`SetFileInformationByHandle(FileRenameInfo)`. The destination is relative to
514696-+the already-held quarantine directory, and replacement is disabled. Entry and
514697-+root exchange tests plant a valid young replacement between classification and
514698-+retirement and assert that it remains a cache hit.
514699-+
514700-+### Runtime orphan compatibility
514701-+
514702-+Orphan matching is limited to manager-owned legacy and indexed temporary and
514703-+backup names plus indexed stale names. PID and allocation indexes must use the
514704-+canonical numeric shape. Live-PID entries and malformed, leading-zero, or
514705-+unrelated dotfiles are retained; only exact dead-PID names are swept.
514706-+
514707-+### Native Windows coverage
514708-+
514709-+The fake build fixture now derives the native target and artifact suffix on
--
514716-+
514717-+The previously accepted currentness behavior was preserved: marker-v1 schemas
514718-+1–5, raw-snapshot and static-context replanning, complete target/toolchain/
514719-+execution-policy cache identity, protected receipt/artifact and shim checks,
514720-+result-only capability evidence, and normal-install rebuild/repair remain
514721-+unchanged by this rework.
514722-+
