519461-+- Exact-head GitHub Actions run: [30679822247](https://github.com/ivanopcode/cocoaskills/actions/runs/30679822247) — **pending at artifact draft time**.
519462-+
519463-+## Reviewer findings resolved
519464-+
519465-+### In-flight journal generations
519466-+
519467-+Transaction journals now expose marker generations in a separate group for
519468-+each context target. A group covers its live, staged, staged-source, backup,
519469-+rollback, cleanup, and cleanup-tomb paths. GC snapshots those paths before and
519470-+after marker reads, requires at least one valid marker in every group, and
519471-+merges references only from a fully safe group. A missing group, corrupt or
519472-+unreadable marker, path race, journal-root race, or journal filesystem error
--
519477-+vanishing, a generation disappearing during the scan, a forced journal-root
519478-+`OSError`, and one valid project target alongside vanished global and hybrid
519479-+targets so unrelated context state cannot mask uncertainty.
519480-+
519481-+### Exact protected-object retirement
519482-+
519483-+The POSIX collector carries the classified directory state into quarantine,
519484-+selects it through the held driver descriptor, and verifies the quarantined
519485-+inode before deletion. A pathname exchange is restored or retained; a driver
519486-+root exchange can sweep only the entry reached through the previously held
519487-+root descriptor and never the new live root.
519488-+
519489-+The Windows collector reopens and records the verified object identity, opens
519490-+the selected source with `DELETE`, and renames that exact open handle with
519491:+`SetFileInformationByHandle(FileRenameInfo)`. The destination is relative to
519492-+the already-held quarantine directory, and replacement is disabled. Entry and
519493-+root exchange tests plant a valid young replacement between classification and
519494-+retirement and assert that it remains a cache hit.
519495-+
519496-+### Runtime orphan compatibility
519497-+
519498-+Orphan matching is limited to manager-owned legacy and indexed temporary and
519499-+backup names plus indexed stale names. PID and allocation indexes must use the
519500-+canonical numeric shape. Live-PID entries and malformed, leading-zero, or
519501-+unrelated dotfiles are retained; only exact dead-PID names are swept.
519502-+
519503-+### Native Windows coverage
519504-+
519505-+The fake build fixture now derives the native target and artifact suffix on
--
519512-+
519513-+The previously accepted currentness behavior was preserved: marker-v1 schemas
519514-+1–5, raw-snapshot and static-context replanning, complete target/toolchain/
519515-+execution-policy cache identity, protected receipt/artifact and shim checks,
519516-+result-only capability evidence, and normal-install rebuild/repair remain
519517-+unchanged by this rework.
519518-+
519519-+## Fact-checking and sources
519520-+
519521-+- The task behavior remains checked against the Curator manager requirements
519522-+  for [status and locked fail-safe GC](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec/blob/f5d7673039226ab81de2f4f87e2155ae995c4df3/profiles/manager.md#L657-L684),
519523-+  [cache acceptance and rebuild](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec/blob/f5d7673039226ab81de2f4f87e2155ae995c4df3/profiles/manager.md#L329-L340),
519524-+  and [normal-install repair](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec/blob/f5d7673039226ab81de2f4f87e2155ae995c4df3/profiles/manager.md#L444-L463).
519525-+- Microsoft documents that the file handle passed to
519526:+  [`SetFileInformationByHandle`](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/fileapi/nf-fileapi-setfileinformationbyhandle)
519527-+  must carry the access needed for the requested change and that
519528-+  `FileRenameInfo` is the rename information class.
519529-+- Microsoft's
519530-+  [`FILE_RENAME_INFORMATION`](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-hardware/drivers/ddi/ntifs/ns-ntifs-_file_rename_information)
519531-+  contract states that rename acts on the supplied file handle, requires
519532-+  `DELETE` access, can resolve a relative name through a held root-directory
519533-+  handle, and fails on an existing target when replacement is false. It also
519534-+  defines the variable-length buffer sizing used by the implementation.
519535-+
