{"files":[{"filename":"sdk-api-src/content/winbase/ns-winbase-file_rename_info.md","patch":"@@ -52,42 +52,43 @@ api_name:\n \n # FILE_RENAME_INFO structure\n \n-\n ## -description\n \n-Contains the name to which the file should be renamed. Use only when calling \n-   \u003ca href=\"/windows/desktop/api/fileapi/nf-fileapi-setfileinformationbyhandle\"\u003eSetFileInformationByHandle\u003c/a\u003e.\n+Contains the target name to which the source file should be renamed. Use only when calling\n+\u003ca href=\"/windows/desktop/api/fileapi/nf-fileapi-setfileinformationbyhandle\"\u003eSetFileInformationByHandle\u003c/a\u003e.\n \n ## -struct-fields\n \n ### -field DUMMYUNIONNAME\n \n ### -field DUMMYUNIONNAME.ReplaceIfExists\n \n-\u003cb\u003eTRUE\u003c/b\u003e to replace the file; otherwise, \u003cb\u003eFALSE\u003c/b\u003e.\n+This field is used when **SetFileInformationByHandle**'s *FileInformationClass* parameter is set to **FileRenameInfo**.\n+If this field is **TRUE** and the target file exists then the target file will be replaced by the source file. If this\n+field is **FALSE** and the target file exists then  operation will return an error.\n \n ### -field DUMMYUNIONNAME.Flags\n \n-### -field ReplaceIfExists\n-\n-\u003cb\u003eTRUE\u003c/b\u003e to replace the file; otherwise, \u003cb\u003eFALSE\u003c/b\u003e.\n+This field is used when **SetFileInformationByHandle**'s *FileInformationClass* parameter is set to **FileRenameInfoEx**.\n \n ### -field RootDirectory\n \n-A handle to the root directory in which the file to be renamed is located.\n+This field should be set to NULL.\n \n ### -field FileNameLength\n \n-The size of \u003cb\u003eFileName\u003c/b\u003e in bytes.\n+The size of **FileName** in bytes, not including the NUL-termination.\n \n ### -field FileName\n \n-The new file name.\n+A NUL-terminated wide-character string containing the new path to the file. The value can be one of the following:\n+\n+- An absolute path (drive, directory, and filename).\n+- A path relative to the process's current directory.\n+- The new name of an NTFS file stream, starting with `:`.\n \n ## -see-also\n \n \u003ca href=\"/windows/desktop/api/minwinbase/ne-minwinbase-file_info_by_handle_class\"\u003eFILE_INFO_BY_HANDLE_CLASS\u003c/a\u003e\n \n-\n-\n-\u003ca href=\"/windows/desktop/api/fileapi/nf-fileapi-setfileinformationbyhandle\"\u003eSetFileInformationByHandle\u003c/a\u003e\n\\ No newline at end of file\n+\u003ca href=\"/windows/desktop/api/fileapi/nf-fileapi-setfileinformationbyhandle\"\u003eSetFileInformationByHandle\u003c/a\u003e","status":"modified"}],"html_url":"https://github.com/MicrosoftDocs/sdk-api/commit/ada04eef90bc7ebe441ce2ef938867d3a677d57d","message":"Merged PR 18437: FILE_RENAME_INFO corrections and clarifications\n\nFILE_RENAME_INFO corrections and clarifications\n\n- **FILE_RENAME_INFO** is used for both `FileRenameInfo` and\n  `FileRenameInfoEx` operations. We need to call out which members of the\n  union are used for each operation. `ReplaceIfExists` is used for\n  `FileRenameInfo` and `Flags` is used for `FileRenameInfoEx`.\n- We need to express what happens if `ReplaceIfExists` is false and the\n  file exists (the operation fails with an error).\n- Fix unnecessarily duplication of `ReplaceIfExists` field in the docs.\n- The `RootDirectory` field is effectively useless in the current\n  implementation. If specified, it does weird and inconsistent things that\n  would be almost impossible to document correctly. In the future maybe the\n  owners of this API might want to fix it. Until then, we should tell\n  people to set it to NULL.\n- FileNameLength needs to be clarified to not include the NUL\n  termination.\n- FileName needs to be clarified that it must be NUL terminated (even\n  though we also require FileNameLength).\n- We also need to clarify what kinds of filenames we accept.","sha":"ada04eef90bc7ebe441ce2ef938867d3a677d57d"}

