+## Reviewer findings resolved
+
+### In-flight journal generations
+
+Transaction journals now expose marker generations in a separate group for
+each context target. A group covers its live, staged, staged-source, backup,
+rollback, cleanup, and cleanup-tomb paths. GC snapshots those paths before and
+after marker reads, requires at least one valid marker in every group, and
+merges references only from a fully safe group. A missing group, corrupt or
+unreadable marker, path race, journal-root race, or journal filesystem error
+makes the whole mark phase uncertain and suppresses runtime, snapshot, and
+build sweeps.
+
+Regression coverage includes an intact staged marker, every generation
+vanishing, a generation disappearing during the scan, a forced journal-root
+`OSError`, and one valid project target alongside vanished global and hybrid
+targets so unrelated context state cannot mask uncertainty.
+
+### Exact protected-object retirement
+
+The POSIX collector carries the classified directory state into quarantine,
+selects it through the held driver descriptor, and verifies the quarantined
+inode before deletion. A pathname exchange is restored or retained; a driver
+root exchange can sweep only the entry reached through the previously held
+root descriptor and never the new live root.
+
+The Windows collector reopens and records the verified object identity, opens
+the selected source with `DELETE`, and renames that exact open handle with
+`SetFileInformationByHandle(FileRenameInfo)`. The destination is relative to
+the already-held quarantine directory, and replacement is disabled. Entry and
+root exchange tests plant a valid young replacement between classification and
+retirement and assert that it remains a cache hit.
+
+### Runtime orphan compatibility
+
+Orphan matching is limited to manager-owned legacy and indexed temporary and
+backup names plus indexed stale names. PID and allocation indexes must use the
+canonical numeric shape. Live-PID entries and malformed, leading-zero, or
+unrelated dotfiles are retained; only exact dead-PID names are swept.
+
+### Native Windows coverage
+
+The fake build fixture now derives the native target and artifact suffix on
+Windows. An unskipped status vector installs through the native protected
+backend and proves a fresh marker-v2 build is current in both the object model
+and JSON. The build-GC grace/mark/sweep integration test also runs natively on
+Windows, while backend tests cover ordinary old/young collection and both
+entry and root exchange races. Test setup temporarily applies the backend's
+mutable ACL profile to age a directory and reseals it before inspection.
+
+The previously accepted currentness behavior was preserved: marker-v1 schemas
+1–5, raw-snapshot and static-context replanning, complete target/toolchain/
+execution-policy cache identity, protected receipt/artifact and shim checks,
+result-only capability evidence, and normal-install rebuild/repair remain
+unchanged by this rework.
+
+## Fact-checking and sources
+
+- The task behavior remains checked against the Curator manager requirements
+  for [status and locked fail-safe GC](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec/blob/f5d7673039226ab81de2f4f87e2155ae995c4df3/profiles/manager.md#L657-L684),
+  [cache acceptance and rebuild](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec/blob/f5d7673039226ab81de2f4f87e2155ae995c4df3/profiles/manager.md#L329-L340),
+  and [normal-install repair](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec/blob/f5d7673039226ab81de2f4f87e2155ae995c4df3/profiles/manager.md#L444-L463).
+- Microsoft documents that the file handle passed to
+  [`SetFileInformationByHandle`](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/fileapi/nf-fileapi-setfileinformationbyhandle)
+  must carry the access needed for the requested change and that
+  `FileRenameInfo` is the rename information class.
+- Microsoft's
+  [`FILE_RENAME_INFORMATION`](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-hardware/drivers/ddi/ntifs/ns-ntifs-_file_rename_information)
+  contract states that rename acts on the supplied file handle, requires
+  `DELETE` access, can resolve a relative name through a held root-directory
+  handle, and fails on an existing target when replacement is false. It also
+  defines the variable-length buffer sizing used by the implementation.
