The exact-head code’s layout is not the fault: on Win64 both the legacy `BOOLEAN` form and modern `DWORD`/union form place `RootDirectory` at 8, `FileNameLength` at 16, and `FileName` at 20; zero-filled padding makes them byte-identical for no-replace. I’m adding a cross-target compiler check so the artifact distinguishes proven ABI facts from the unavailable live-host matrix.
